   rubric:"Structure — keeping a long list organised without losing a line.",
   ask:["What does the dinosaur bring in beyond tickets?","What does it cost to keep?"],
   watch:"Nine numbers read out loud. Write them in two columns before you add anything.",
   attempt:{q:"Ask line by line and you are told — revenues: tickets $2.0M, hotels $1.0M, licensing $0.5M, park food $0.5M, merchandise "
              +"$0.25M, research $0.25M. Costs: staff $1.0M, food and merchandise $0.25M, operations "
              +"$0.25M. What is the annual profit?",
            a:"$4.5M of revenue less $1.5M of cost, so $3.0M a year for 29 years. Flat — the case says "
             +"to treat revenues and costs as static."},
   src:"Annual revenue: $2M tickets + $1M hotel + $0.5M movie + $0.5M park food + $0.25M merchandise + "
      +"$0.25M research = $4.5M. Annual costs: $1M staff + $0.25M food & merchandise + $0.25M "
